<title>UK: KDB sets $300 million five-year FRN.</title>
<headline>KDB sets $300 million five-year FRN.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following floating-rate issue was announced by lead manager Goldman Sachs International.</p>
<p> BORROWER   KOREA DEVELOPMENT BANK</p>
<p> AMT	  $300 MLN  BASE	 3M-LIBOR  MATURITY	 JUN.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 MARGIN     +18.75 BP PAY DATE    30.JUN.97</p>
<p> MOODY	A1	  ISS PRICE  99.95     FULL FEES   =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA-	 REOFFER    99.95</p>
<p> NOTES     *CALLABLE AT PAR AFTER THREE YEARS.</p>
<p>		PUT OPTION ON COUPON DATES IN THE EVENT OF RATINGS</p>
<p>		FALLING BELOW EITHER A3 OR A-.</p>
<p> LISTING    LONDON    DENOMS (K) 10-100    SALE LIMITS US/GB</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  KOREA     TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.10	SELL CONC  0.05	PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
